    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Vape Device Temperature Warning: How to Protect Your Cartridges & Disposables"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>As summer heats up on Cape Cod, it’s more important than ever to store your <b>vape devices</b> safely. Whether you’re using <a href=\"/categories/vaporizers/\"><b>cannabis cartridges</b></a> or <a href=\"/categories/vaporizers/disposables/\"><b>disposable vapes</b></a>, improper storage—especially in extreme temperatures—can damage your device and pose safety risks.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Why You Should Never Leave Vapes in a Hot Car?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>It might feel like a mild 80°F outside, but inside your car, temperatures can soar well over 100°F. When left in these conditions, <b>vape devices</b> are at risk of:</p><ul><li><p><b>Leaking oil</b> from heat expansion</p></li><li><p><b>Battery malfunction</b> or sluggish performance</p></li><li><p><b>Melting, warping</b>, or—though rare—<b>explosions</b></p></li></ul><p>Many vape pens and disposables use <b>lithium-ion batteries</b>, just like your laptop or phone. These batteries are sensitive to both high heat and freezing cold, and they should always be stored with care.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "What are the Vape battery Safety Risks from Temperature Extremes?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>Exposure to high or low temperatures can result in:</p><ul><li><p>Batteries <b>losing efficiency</b> or <b>stopping altogether</b></p></li><li><p><b>Permanent device damage</b></p></li><li><p><b>Safety hazards</b> due to battery failure or overheating</p></li></ul><p>Moisture, such as rain or condensation, can also short-circuit your vape or degrade the battery. Avoid leaving your vape anywhere it’s exposed to water or extreme humidity—like glove compartments, beach bags, or window sills.</p>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "What are the Best Practices for Vape Storage?"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>To keep your <b>cannabis vape pens, cartridges, and disposables</b> in top condition:</p><ul><li><p>Store between <b>14°F and 86°F</b> (ideal range for lithium-ion batteries)</p></li><li><p>Avoid <b>direct sunlight</b>, especially through glass</p></li><li><p>Keep devices <b>dry</b>, away from rain, snow, or moisture</p></li><li><p>Don’t leave them in parked cars, beach bags, or backpacks left in the sun</p></li></ul>"
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": 3,
     "text": "Vape Smart with Cape Cod Cannabis"
    },
    {
     "t": "rich",
     "html": "<p>At Cape Cod Cannabis, we want every product to meet your expectations. That’s why it’s important to know: <b>devices damaged due to improper storage or neglect cannot be returned or exchanged</b>.</p><p>If you’re unsure how to store your vape—or if it’s safe to use—<b>ask a product specialist</b> at our Wellfleet dispensary. We’re here to help you vape safely and get the most out of every product.</p><p><b><br>Cape Cod Cannabis Dispensary – Your Trusted Source for Vape Products &amp; Cannabis Education.</b></p><p>Protect your device. Vape smart. Visit us today for the <a href=\"/categories/vaporizers/\">best cannabis vapes</a> on Cape Cod!</p>"
    }
   ]
  },
